# Line endings are repo policy, not a per-machine setting.
#
# Every blob in this repository is committed with LF. Without this file, a clone
# on Windows with core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' default) checks those
# blobs out as CRLF. That is invisible for source Git normalizes on commit, but
# it broke a generated-artifact guard: tests/apiSurface.test.ts compares
# docs/openapi.json against a freshly generated string, and the generator emits
# LF, so the comparison failed on every Windows working tree while passing on
# the Linux CI runner — reporting a stale spec when the spec was current.
#
# eol=lf pins the *working tree* to LF regardless of core.autocrlf, so what a
# test reads off disk is what was committed on any platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never translate, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.sqlite binary
